<% content_for :title, "CLI — Shadwire" %>
<% content_for :description, "The complete shadwire CLI reference: init, add, list, search, info, diff, update, remove and status, with every flag, the JSON payload and how errors are reported." %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <%= tag.style rouge_stylesheet %>
<% end %>

<article class="space-y-12">
  <%= render "docs/header",
        title: "CLI",
        description: "The development-time tool that installs component source into your app and keeps it in step with the registry." %>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <p class="leading-7">
      After <%= link_to "init", docs_installation_path, class: "font-medium underline underline-offset-4" %>,
      every command goes through <%= docs_code("bin/shadwire") %>. The binstub resolves through
      the app's bundle, so everyone runs the same version of the CLI. Each command carries its
      own help under <%= docs_code("bin/shadwire help COMMAND") %>.
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:quick_reference], language: :shell) %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Commands") %>

    <%= render "docs/table",
          headers: [ "Command", "What it does" ],
          rows: @commands.map { |command|
            [ docs_code(command[:signature]), command[:summary] ]
          } %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-8">
    <%= docs_h2("Reference") %>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <%= docs_h3("status") %>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        The project's context in a single call. It is the command to run first, and the only one
        an agent needs to inject.
      </p>
      <%= docs_code_block("bin/shadwire status --json", language: :shell) %>
      <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:status_json], language: :json) %>

      <%= render "docs/table",
            headers: [ "Field", "How to read it" ],
            rows: [
              [ docs_code("installed[].helpers"), "The ui_* methods that actually exist in this app. Calling a helper for a component that is not installed raises NoMethodError." ],
              [ docs_code("installed[].drift"), safe_join([ docs_code("unchanged"), ", ", docs_code("modified"), ", ", docs_code("missing"), " or ", docs_code("unknown"), "." ]) ],
              [ docs_code("stack.importmap"), "Whether importmap and Stimulus are present. The interactive components need both." ],
              [ docs_code("cli.binstub"), safe_join([ "Whether ", docs_code("bin/shadwire"), " exists yet. False means running ", docs_code("init"), " once." ]) ],
              [ docs_code("helpers.includeAllHelpers"), safe_join([ "False means the app turned off Rails' automatic helper inclusion: the ", docs_code("Ui::*Helper"), " modules then need a ", docs_code("helper"), " call per controller." ]) ],
              [ docs_code("helpers.legacyHelperPresent"), safe_join([ "An ", docs_code("app/helpers/ui_helper.rb"), " left over from before the split by component. It defines helpers for components you do not have installed; it is safe to delete." ]) ]
            ] %>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <%= docs_h3("search") %>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        The search matches name, title, description <strong class="font-medium text-foreground">and</strong>
        the when-to-use text, so conceptual terms work:
        <%= docs_code("form") %>, <%= docs_code("modal") %>, <%= docs_code("overlay") %>,
        <%= docs_code("loading") %>, <%= docs_code("right-click") %>.
      </p>
      <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:search], language: :shell) %>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <%= docs_h3("info") %>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        The component's full API. Read it before writing ERB instead of guessing at a prop. It
        returns <%= docs_code("whenToUse") %>, <%= docs_code("usage") %> snippets,
        <%= docs_code("requiresStimulus") %>, <%= docs_code("registryDependencies") %>, the
        install files, and <%= docs_code("api.components[]") %> with each class's helper,
        variants, sizes, props and attributes.
      </p>
      <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:info], language: :shell) %>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        <%= docs_code("helper") %> comes back <%= docs_code("null") %> for anything without a
        <%= docs_code("ui_*") %> wrapper: the base superclass, the internal parts a parent
        renders on its own, and the blocks. File bodies are omitted.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <%= docs_h3("add") %>
      <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:add], language: :shell) %>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        Without <%= docs_code("--yes") %>, files identical to the registry are skipped silently
        and only the locally modified ones prompt. In a non-interactive shell without
        <%= docs_code("--yes") %>, everything is skipped and nothing gets installed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <%= docs_h3("diff") %>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        Read-only. Reports <%= docs_code("unchanged") %> / <%= docs_code("modified") %> /
        <%= docs_code("missing") %> per file, with a unified diff for the modified ones.
      </p>
      <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:diff], language: :shell) %>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <%= docs_h3("update") %>
      <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:update], language: :shell) %>
      <%= render layout: "docs/callout", locals: { icon: "triangle-alert", variant: :destructive, title: "update overwrites local edits" } do %>
        Run <code>diff</code> first. <code>update</code> does report what it replaced
        (<code>overwritten</code> and <code>diffs</code> in the JSON payload), but that is after
        the fact. See <a href="<%= docs_theming_path %>#keeping-your-edits" class="font-medium underline underline-offset-4">how to keep your edits</a>.
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <%= docs_h3("remove") %>
      <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:remove], language: :shell) %>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        It deletes only the files exclusive to the components being removed. The shared base,
        and any file another installed component still uses, stays where it is. Importmap pins
        nobody uses any more are reported, not removed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Flags") %>

    <%= render "docs/table",
          headers: [ "Flag", "Commands", "Effect" ],
          rows: @flags.map { |flag| [ docs_code(flag[:flag]), flag[:commands], flag[:description] ] } %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Errors and exit codes") %>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Exit code 0 means it worked. A command that could not install a dependency says so and
      exits non-zero, so you can trust the exit code instead of re-reading the Gemfile.
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:errors], language: :console) %>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Each error comes out as one actionable line on stderr. A malformed
      <%= docs_code("shadwire.json") %>, an unreachable registry, a registry serving HTML and a
      missing argument each produce their own:
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:error_messages], language: :text) %>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      The exception is <%= docs_code("status") %>, which never fails: it reports
      <%= docs_code('"rails": false') %>, <%= docs_code("registryError") %> or
      <%= docs_code("configError") %> as fields and exits 0. That is what makes it safe to
      inject anywhere.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("In CI") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Every command runs non-interactively with <%= docs_code("--yes") %>, emits JSON with
      <%= docs_code("--json") %>, and points at another directory with <%= docs_code("--cwd") %>.
      This recipe fails the build when an installed component has diverged from the registry:
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:ci], language: :yaml) %>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      The job needs the <%= docs_code("development") %> group installed; without it,
      <%= docs_code("bin/shadwire") %> does not exist.
    </p>
  </section>
</article>
